# Canonical author identity.
#
# Seven early commits were authored with a personal Gmail address before the
# GitHub noreply alias was configured. Rewriting history to remove it would
# change every commit SHA in the repository -- breaking every clone, every
# open pull request and every existing link to a commit -- to hide an address
# that is already public on those same commits upstream.
#
# A mailmap is the non-destructive half of that fix: git log, git shortlog,
# git blame and GitHub's own contributor views all read it, so the personal
# address stops being what anyone sees, while the commits themselves are left
# alone. It does not remove the address from the raw commit objects. If the
# raw objects have to be scrubbed too, that is `git filter-repo --mailmap`
# with this same file, on a fresh clone, followed by a force push.
#
# Going forward the alias is set per-clone:
#   git config user.email 64616761+keldessouky@users.noreply.github.com

